# The dashboard's environment under compose — install as
# ~/fq-dogfood/.secrets/dashboard.env (chmod 600). A plain KEY=VALUE
# file: compose does no shell expansion.
#
# This is a SEPARATE file from .secrets/env on purpose (#545): the
# dashboard is the one web-facing process and it holds exactly the three
# edge settings it reads plus its own tuning — never a provider key,
# never GH_TOKEN, never the broker token. Under the setsid launchers
# dashboard.sh achieved this by starting the binary under `env -i`; under
# compose the file boundary is the mechanism.

# The daemon's edge as the dashboard reaches it. The daemon's container
# publishes its edge on host loopback and the dashboard runs on the host
# network, so this is the published address, not the container's.
FQ_EDGE=127.0.0.1:9470

# The daemon's certificate fingerprint (SHA-256, hex) — <state>/edge/
# fingerprint inside the instance volume; the daemon prints it at first
# start. Rotating the daemon's identity invalidates it, and every issued
# token with it.
FQ_EDGE_FINGERPRINT=REPLACE-ME

# An ATTENUATED token — the seven reads the pages render, never the admin
# token. Mint it from the admin token (README, "The dashboard's
# identity"):
#
#   fq token attenuate --addr "$FQ_EDGE" \
#     --grant read:agent --grant read:control --grant read:cost \
#     --grant read:event --grant read:invocation \
#     --grant read:operator_signal --grant read:turn
#
# read:operator_signal is the notifications pane's, and is newer than the
# other six: a token minted without it leaves the pane refused and the
# home page's notification row reading `unknown`. Re-mint, then recreate
# the dashboard (an env_file is read only on create).
FQ_EDGE_TOKEN=REPLACE-ME

# Where the dashboard serves (loopback only; Caddy proxies to it) and how
# often its pages refresh, in seconds. Defaults shown.
# FQ_DASHBOARD_BIND=127.0.0.1:9472
# FQ_DASHBOARD_REFRESH=5
